---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Calculator from '../components/tools/Calculator.svelte';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="A calorie starting point"
  description="An educational Mifflin–St Jeor calorie tool with metric and imperial inputs."
  ><section class="page-intro">
    <p class="mono">The calorie calculator</p><h1>A starting point.<br />With the workings.</h1><p>
      Estimate your daily energy needs, understand the assumptions, and carry the result into the demo.
    </p>
  </section><Calculator client:load /><article class="reading">
    <h2>Here’s the equation.</h2><p>
      Mifflin–St Jeor estimates resting energy: 10 × weight in kg + 6.25 × height in cm − 5 × age, plus 5 for the male
      constant or minus 161 for the female constant. Multiply by the chosen activity factor to estimate maintenance.
    </p><p>
      A selected small deficit subtracts 250 kcal; a small surplus adds 250 kcal. These are demo adjustments. They are
      not part of the original resting-energy equation.
    </p><p>
      The formula predicts a population-level estimate. It is not a measurement, diagnosis or individual dietary
      prescription. The tool is an adult educational example.
    </p><p>
      Equation source: <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/2305711/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
        >Mifflin et al., 1990, A new predictive equation for resting energy expenditure</a
      >.
    </p><a href="/busog/quiz/">Prefer a short guided quiz? ↗</a>
  </article></SiteLayout
>
